`ifndef HISI_VDP_AV100_RDL
`define HISI_VDP_AV100_RDL


regfile eHISI_VDP_AV100 {
    name = "HiSilicon video display processor (Hi3516A/D V100)";
    desc = "
    HiSilicon video display processor (VDP) of the Hi3516A V100 / Hi3516D V100 at 0x205C0000 (interrupt 65 on the GIC-400). Video layer V1 (the data sheet documents V1 at 0x1000; the vendor header lists the V0 layer at 0x0800 with the same layout plus 16 regions and DCMP state), graphics layers G0 (header, 0x6000) and G2 (data sheet, 0x7000), display channels DHD0 (header, 0xC000) and DHD1 (data sheet, 0xC400), BT.1120/BT.656 interface registers (BT_* 0xD200, INTF_* 0xD000) and the DATE TV encoder (0xF2xx). Global VOCTRL/VOINTSTA/VOMSKINTSTA/VOINTMSK/VDPVERSION/VO_MUX at 0x0 and the VO DAC control at 0x130. Non-instant registers take effect after the layer/channel `*_UPD` bit, as on the Hi3520D VDP (`eHISI_VDP`). Generation: same register family as the Hi3518E V20X `eHISI_VDP_V2` (79 of its 81 registers appear here) and the Hi3516C V300 / Hi3516A V200 / Hi3519 VDPs.

    Generated 2026-11-10 by build/rdl-audit/video-rdl-scratch/gen_blocks.py: mechanical transcription of the data sheet register tables (ds_extract2 + description extraction from the PDF) merged with the vendor header; not hardware verified.

    Register sources: 153 registers from the data sheet (hi3516av100--Hi3516A-Hi3516D-Datasheet.txt, section 10.2.6); 104 registers and 72 fields from vendor U-Boot 2010.06 `product/hiosd/vo/hi3516a/vou_reg.h` (GPL-2.0 U-Boot tree, HiSilicon copyright, created 2013-04-27; mirror github.com/OpenIPC/u-boot-hi3516cv200) (GPL-2.0, same-chip vendor header), each marked `[inferred]` in its desc (names from the header, meanings inferred from the names, reset/access unknown). Name differences, data sheet kept: 0x4 VOINTSTA [19:19] DS v1_dc_err_int / header v3rr_int; 0x8 VOMSKINTSTA [19:19] DS v1_dc_err_int / header v3rr_clr; 0xC VOINTMSK [19:19] DS v1_dc_err_int / header v3rr_intmsk; 0x100 VO_MUX [27:27] DS yc_sel / header ye_sel; 0xF318 name DS DATE_COEFF70 / header DATE_COEFF71; 0xF31C name DS DATE_COEFF71 / header DATE_COEFF72; 0xF31C DATE_COEFF71 header field phase_shift_coeff [31:0] overlaps DS fields differently; 0xF320 name DS DATE_COEFF72 / header DATE_COEFF73; 0xF320 DATE_COEFF72 header field coef_notch_ovrd [0:0] overlaps DS fields differently; 0xF324 name DS DATE_COEFF73 / header DATE_COEFF74; 0xF324 DATE_COEFF73 header field coef_notch_1 [9:0] overlaps DS fields differently; 0xF328 name DS DATE_COEFF74 / header DATE_COEFF75; 0xF328 DATE_COEFF74 [9:0] DS coef_notch_1 / header coef_notch_3; 0xF328 DATE_COEFF74 [25:16] DS coef_notch_2 / header coef_notch_4; 0xF32C name DS DATE_COEFF75 / header DATE_COEFF76; 0xF32C DATE_COEFF75 [9:0] DS coef_notch_3 / header coef_notch_5; 0xF32C DATE_COEFF75 [25:16] DS coef_notch_4 / header coef_notch_6; 0xF330 name DS DATE_COEFF76 / header DATE_COEFF77; 0xF330 DATE_COEFF76 [9:0] DS coef_notch_5 / header coef_notch_7; 0xF330 DATE_COEFF76 [25:16] DS coef_notch_6 / header coef_notch_8; 0xF334 name DS DATE_COEFF77 / header DATE_COEFF78; 0xF334 DATE_COEFF77 [9:0] DS coef_notch_7 / header coef_notch_9; 0xF334 DATE_COEFF77 [25:16] DS coef_notch_8 / header coef_notch_10; 0xF338 name DS DATE_COEFF78 / header DATE_COEFF79; 0xF338 DATE_COEFF78 [9:0] DS coef_notch_9 / header coef_notch_11; 0xF338 DATE_COEFF78 [25:16] DS coef_notch_10 / header coef_notch_12; 0xF33C name DS DATE_COEFF79 / header DATE_COEFF80; 0xF33C DATE_COEFF79 header field coef_chra_lpf_ovrd [0:0] overlaps DS fields differently; 0xF340 name DS DATE_COEFF80 / header DATE_COEFF81; 0xF340 DATE_COEFF80 header field coef_chra_lpf_1 [8:0] overlaps DS fields differently; 0xF344 name DS DATE_COEFF81 / header DATE_COEFF82; 0xF344 DATE_COEFF81 [8:0] DS coef_chra_lpf_1 / header coef_chra_lpf_3; 0xF344 DATE_COEFF81 [24:16] DS coef_chra_lpf_2 / header coef_chra_lpf_4; 0xF348 name DS DATE_COEFF82 / header DATE_COEFF83; 0xF348 DATE_COEFF82 [8:0] DS coef_chra_lpf_3 / header coef_chra_lpf_5; 0xF348 DATE_COEFF82 [24:16] DS coef_chra_lpf_4 / header coef_chra_lpf_6; 0xF34C name DS DATE_COEFF83 / header DATE_COEFF84; 0xF34C DATE_COEFF83 [8:0] DS coef_chra_lpf_5 / header coef_chra_lpf_7; header register BT_CTRL at 0xD000 renamed BT_CTRL_D000 (name used by the data sheet elsewhere).";

